# Cursor Rules — Freerouting C++ Migration

## Project Context
Migrating Freerouting PCB autorouter from Java to C++20. Java source is truth. Headless routing parity goal.

## At Session Start
Read `SOURCE_OF_TRUTH/01_MEMORY.md` and `SOURCE_OF_TRUTH/05_WORK_PACKAGES.md`.

## Build
```bash
cmake --build build --target <module_target> -j$(nproc)
ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure
```

## Rules
1. Java `src/**/*.java` is reference — port faithfully
2. 4 files per class: `.h`, `.cpp`, `_test.cpp`, `.java`
3. C++20: smart pointers, RAII, `std::optional`, `#pragma once`
4. Naming: PascalCase classes, snake_case functions, trailing `_` for private
5. Layering: `freerouting_core` has NO deps
6. Never include `src/board/Components.h/.cpp` — dead code
7. Java nets are 1-based for indexing

## Gotchas
- `Item::get_normal_contacts()` base returns `{}` — Trace overrides
- `DrillItem` canonical = `Via.h`
- No JSON serializer — hand-roll matching Java `@SerializedName`
- `run_tests` AND `ctest` must both pass

## Session End
Update `SOURCE_OF_TRUTH/02_PROGRESS.md`, `03_MISSING.md`, `docs/migration/INDEX.md`.
